@* When an activity's encounter happened (T137, from T119's ObservedOn): a list cell, and the activity page's summary
   (T161). A date nobody stated is only the day the form was created, and it says so ("not recorded (created …)", T197)
   rather than passing the audit clock off as a clinical fact. The wording is EncounterDate.Label, shared with the
   trajectory, the portfolio PDF and the committee's evidence summary (D28).
   It is visible text, not a tooltip: a keyboard, touch or screen-reader user never sees a title. *@
<span class="@(Declared ? null : "muted")">@EncounterDate.Label(ObservedOn, Declared)</span>

@code {
  [Parameter, EditorRequired] public DateOnly ObservedOn { get; set; }
  [Parameter] public bool Declared { get; set; }
}
